.TH CUPS-FILES.CONF 5 "2026-11-18" "Presswork 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
cups\-files.conf \- file, directory, privilege, and sandboxing configuration for Presswork cupsd
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.I cups\-files.conf
file configures filesystem paths, file permissions, service accounts,
environment filtering, device policy, and filter/backend sandboxing for
.BR cupsd (8).
It is normally located at
.I /etc/cups/cups\-files.conf
with mode
.B 0640
owned by
.BR root:lp .
.PP
Keeping path and privilege directives separate from
.BR cupsd.conf (5)
prevents administrative HTTP edits to
.I cupsd.conf
from altering executable directories, log paths, or privilege boundaries.
Verify changes with
.B cupsd \-\-check\-config
and
.BR "cupsd doctor" .
.SH DIRECTIVES
.SS Accounts & Permissions
.TP
.BI User " username|uid"
Unprivileged user account under which filters, backends, and helper processes
execute (shipped default:
.BR lp ).
Presswork flags UID 0 as
.B ROOT_WORKER_USER
and refuses to run filters as root.
.TP
.BI Group " groupname|gid"
Primary group under which filters, backends, and helper processes execute
(shipped default:
.BR lp ).
.TP
.BI SystemGroup " group [group ...]"
Space-separated Unix groups granted
.B @SYSTEM
administrative privileges (shipped default:
.BR lpadmin ;
code fallback:
.BR "sys root wheel lpadmin" ).
.B Important:
Never add the
.B lp
user to
.BR lpadmin .
.TP
.BI SystemGroupAuthKey " key"
macOS authorization key (parsed for compatibility; unused on Linux).
.TP
.BI RemoteRoot " username"
Username mapped to unauthenticated remote root requests (default:
.BR remroot ).
.TP
.BI ConfigFilePerm " mode"
Octal permissions applied to written configuration files such as
.I printers.conf
and
.I classes.conf
(default:
.BR 0640 ).
.TP
.BI LogFilePerm " mode"
Octal permissions applied to log files (shipped default:
.BR 0640 ).
.TP
.BI LogFileGroup " group|gid"
Optional group ownership for log files.
.SS Directory Layout
.TP
.BI ServerRoot " directory"
Configuration root directory (default:
.IR /etc/cups ).
Must exist at parse time.
.TP
.BI ServerBin " directory"
Root directory for helper daemons
.RI ( daemon/ ),
backends
.RI ( backend/ ),
filters
.RI ( filter/ ),
and CGIs
.RI ( cgi\-bin/ )
(default:
.IR /usr/lib/cups ).
Must exist at parse time.
.TP
.BI DataDir " directory"
Shared read-only data root containing
.IR mime/ ,
.IR banners/ ,
.IR drv/ ,
and
.I ppd/
(default:
.IR /usr/share/cups ).
.TP
.BI DocumentRoot " directory"
Static web document root (unified default:
.IR /usr/share/cups/doc\-root ).
When empty and
.B WebInterface Yes
is set,
.BR cupsd (8)
serves its built-in read-only HTML status interface.
.TP
.BI RequestRoot " directory"
Job spool directory storing
.I c*
control and
.I d*
document files (default:
.IR /var/spool/cups ,
mode 0710, lp:lp).
.TP
.BI CacheDir " directory"
Cache directory for
.I job.cache
and derived state (default:
.IR /var/cache/cups ,
mode 0770, lp:lp).
.TP
.BI StateDir " directory"
Runtime state directory for certificates and Unix sockets (default:
.IR /run/cups ,
mode 0755, lp:lp).
.TP
.BI TempDir " directory"
Temporary directory for spooled HTTP request bodies and filter scratch files
(default:
.IR RequestRoot/tmp ).
Must exist if explicitly configured.
.TP
.BI ServerKeychain " directory"
Directory storing TLS certificate
.RI ( server.crt )
and private key
.RI ( server.key )
(default:
.IR /etc/cups/ssl ,
mode 0700, root:root).
.SS Logs
.TP
.BI AccessLog " filename|syslog|stderr"
Path for HTTP/IPP access log (default:
.IR /var/log/cups/access_log ).
.TP
.BI ErrorLog " filename|syslog|stderr"
Path for scheduler error and diagnostic log (default:
.IR /var/log/cups/error_log ).
.TP
.BI PageLog " filename|syslog|stderr"
Path for per-page accounting log (default:
.IR /var/log/cups/page_log ).
.SS Security, Sandboxing & Device Policy
.TP
.BI Sandboxing " strict|relaxed|off"
Controls Linux Landlock and sandbox policy enforced by
.B cups\-exec
for filter and backend child processes (code default:
.BR strict ;
shipped
.I cups\-files.conf.default
sets
.BR relaxed
for broad third-party filter compatibility).
Both
.B strict
and
.B relaxed
enforce privilege drop,
.BR "umask 077" ,
.BR setrlimit (2),
and
.BR PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS .
Setting
.B off
is flagged as
.B SANDBOXING_OFF
by
.BR "cupsd \-\-check\-config" .
.TP
.BI FileDevice " Yes|No|^regex$"
Controls whether
.B file://
device URIs are permitted (default:
.BR No ,
strictly enforced fail-closed in both
.B cupsd
and
.BR cups\-backend\-file ).
Setting
.B Yes
permits
.B ^/dev/tty[A\-Za\-z0\-9._]+$
or specify an explicit anchored regex pattern.
Enabling
.B FileDevice
is flagged as
.B FILE_DEVICE_ENABLED
by
.BR "cupsd \-\-check\-config" .
.TP
.BI PeerCred " On|Off|RootOnly"
Controls kernel
.B SO_PEERCRED
authentication over Unix domain sockets (default:
.BR On ).
.TP
.BI CreateSelfSignedCerts " Yes|No"
Allow automatic self-signed TLS certificate generation in
.B ServerKeychain
only when both
.I server.crt
and
.I server.key
are absent (default:
.BR Yes ).
Set
.B No
when deploying CA-managed certificates.
Presswork never overwrites existing certificates on parse error.
.TP
.BI PassEnv " var [var ...]"
Allowlist of environment variables forwarded from
.B cupsd
to child processes.
Security-sensitive variables \(en including all
.B LD_*
dynamic-linker variables,
.BR PATH ,
.BR IFS ,
.BR BASH_ENV ,
.BR ENV ,
.BR GCONV_PATH ,
.BR PYTHONPATH ,
.BR PERL5LIB ,
.BR RUBYLIB ,
.BR NODE_OPTIONS ,
.BR HTTP_PROXY ,
.BR HTTPS_PROXY ,
.BR ALL_PROXY ,
.BR DEVICE_URI ,
and internal
.B CUPS_*
/
.B AUTH_*
variables \(en are strictly prohibited and rejected at parse time.
.TP
.BI SetEnv " var value"
Set an explicit environment variable for child processes (for example,
.B "SetEnv CUPS_ALLOW_LOOPBACK_BACKENDS yes"
to opt into loopback backend connections).
Subject to the same prohibited variable list as
.BR PassEnv .
.SS Miscellaneous & Compatibility
.TP
.BI Printcap " [filename]"
Path to legacy printcap file (shipped default:
.IR /run/cups/printcap ).
Parsed for compatibility.
.TP
.BI PrintcapFormat " bsd|plist|solaris"
Format for legacy printcap output (default:
.BR bsd ).
.TP
.BI StripUserDomain " Yes|No"
Strip
.I @domain
suffixes from authenticated usernames (default:
.BR No ).
.TP
.BI SyncOnClose " Yes|No"
Call
.BR fsync (2)
before closing written state/config files (default:
.BR No ;
atomic spool and config writes always sync safely).
.TP
.BI FatalErrors " none|all|browse|config|listen|log|permissions"
Specify which configuration diagnostic classes abort startup.
.TP
.BI OAuthServer " url"
.TQ
.BI OAuthScopes " scopes"
.TQ
.BI OAuthGroup " name filename"
Parsed for CUPS 2.5 compatibility (built-in OIDC provider adapters are planned;
custom
.B TokenVerifier
integrations use
.BR crates/authn ).
.SH DEPRECATED DIRECTIVES
.TP
.BR ServerCertificate ", " ServerKey
Deprecated upstream; use
.B ServerKeychain
instead (flagged by
.BR "cupsd \-\-check\-config" ).
.SH FILES
.I /etc/cups/cups\-files.conf
.br
.I /etc/cups/cups\-files.conf.default
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cupsd (8),
.BR cupsd.conf (5),
.BR cupsfilter (8),
.BR cups\-lpd (8)
